SOURCE AND MECHANISM
lab/web/harness-icon.html:12 — explicit 12,16,20,32,64 size loop; :13 — tinted32.
lab/web/components.js:61 — canonical currentColor SVG dictionary; :62-71 — compound paths, analytic circle/rrect primitives and sidebar divider.
crates/bboxybook/build.rs:16 — regex reads those exact SVG strings; :20-22 — adds the namespace and replaces currentColor with white. Native uses the same geometry as the lab.
crates/bbt-ui/src/atoms.rs:84 — Icon::paint forwards rect/name/context color without a raster-size decision.
crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/icons.rs:70 — RasterKey includes name, requested physical size and DPR; :153 — cache lookup/raster, :180 — resvg renders at that exact size. Existing code already retains independent per-size device rasters; this is NOT a first-raster-size reuse defect.
crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/mod.rs:541 — Prim::Icon requests device-size raster; :555-556 — accepted CSS half-up origin snap before DPR. No changed layout or origin rule is indicated.
crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/chrome.wgsl:24 — premultiplied atlas sampling/tint is correct; the CPU control below reproduces the complete existing native RGB exactly.
Observed cause: web compound paths expose quarter-coverage steps, while native resvg/tiny-skia coverage is continuous. Web circle/rounded-box edges are continuous rather than quarter-stepped. This is raster coverage, not SVG path/font hinting, a colour/tint error or incorrect scaling. The browser renderer backend was not traced; Chrome/Metal 4x attribution is supported by the coverage pattern, the direct Metal sample query, and the diagnostic emulation, not by a GPU trace.
At 64 px the web claude/codex/pi crops have only 9 RGB colours (background checker plus 0/quarter/half/three-quarter/full edge coverage). Native has more intermediate levels. The analytical basic-shape control clears omp's >8 deltas at every tested size in both themes without changing its geometry.

