Diagnostic control: opaque path coverage rendered without AA on a 4x quarter grid, then the four Metal positions resolved per output pixel. Separate generic circle/rrect/single-segment line controls use pixel-centre distance coverage clamped to [0,1], preserving stroke width, cap and source-over. No per-icon name or size adjustment, and no tolerance adjustment. Combining those controls predicts 0 reviews / 2723 changed pixels across 56 pages. That is causal evidence only: the alternate sampling was rejected, not shipped, and is not an achieved parity result. Other probe patterns (mirrored 4x, regular 2x2, box16, implicit-rrect variants) were diagnostic alternatives, not repeated acceptance gates.
Exact symbols were sent before editing in DM 095d5714-ae45-4272-af3f-eb2d75ce9d65. A draft icon_raster.rs plus icons.rs integration/module declaration was temporarily written, then removed on the ruling. Existing tracked renderer files were restored from HEAD; the untracked new helper was removed. A copy is retained only under ignored target/f1-a9436af/discarded-draft for provenance. No text/path shadow atlas, WGSL, glyph cache or UI atom edit remains. Sable was notified that the RGBA proposal did not overlap MK1's R8 path/text masks.
The draft cargo check was interrupted on this ruling. It is not frozen-source validation: source was restored while dependencies were still checking. Only the recorded owned cargo PID and its recorded descendants were stopped; target/f1-a9436af/check-native-stop.json records PID ancestry and signals.

REQUESTED VISUAL JUDGEMENT
Oracle requested native vs web Claude/Codex at 32 CSS px, shown at 2x. Viewed inspection/claude-codex-32-dark-2x.png and -light-2x.png, WEB left / NATIVE right, nearest-neighbour 2x magnification of DPR1 accepted captures. These are not fresh DPR2 captures.
My judgement: native is at least as good in both themes. Claude's diagonal and rounded-cap transitions are smoother; Codex preserves the same sharp hexagon and inner mark with less stepped edge coverage. No missing detail or colour problem is visible. Codex is close at this scale; the difference is edge smoothness, not a different mark. Keep native's smoother raster and leave all 48 as named reference artifacts. This is visual judgement, separate from deterministic measurements.

